  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 130,
    "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
    "note": "IEEE 802.3at PoE+ on twelve of the twenty-four copper ports at up to 30 W per port against a 130 W total budget; the other twelve ports carry no power at all. The datasheet states counts only (12 x GbE PoE RJ-45 ports, 12 x GbE RJ-45 ports) and neither the datasheet text layer nor the series user guide names which port numbers form the PSE group, so ports 1-12 are modelled as the PoE group following the model list left-to-right order. That numbering is the one inferred field in this spec; the counts, the standard and the 130 W budget are cited. 130 W cannot fill twelve 30 W ports, so the budget binds before the port count does."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 48000,
    "kind": "switching capacity",
    "note": "Zyxel quotes 48 Gbps switching capacity and 35.7 Mpps forwarding rate, with a 525 K packet buffer, an 8 K MAC address table and 9 K jumbo frames."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
  "notes": "Zyxel GS1900 Series datasheet (dated 16/11/22) https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf; specification table https://www.zyxel.com/global/en/products/switch/gs1900-series/specification. Management and switching features from the datasheet feature list and the GS1900 Series User Guide V2.90 Edition 2 https://download.zyxel.com/GS1900-48HPv2/user_guide/GS1900-48HPv2_V2.90_Ed2.pdf. There is NO console port and no CLI anywhere in the series: management is the web GUI, SNMP v1/v2/v3, RMON 1/2/3/9, syslog, LLDP/LLDP-MED, 802.1x, RADIUS and TACACS+, which is why no device here declares cli. Twenty-four-port PoE model: total port count 24, of which 12 are 802.3at PoE ports, no SFP, 130 W budget, 166.5 W maximum consumption, 330 x 230 x 44 mm, 2.48 kg, smart fan (19 dBA idle / 40 dBA maximum) - the first model in the line that is not fanless."
